// The tool palette, as data (docs/slices/S18.md §2; docs/design/workspace.md §3). Each tool is a
// behaviour the code knows (Select, Translate, Place, Probe); its key is the action `tool <id>` in
// ui/actions.ron, so the keys, the ? sheet and the command palette have it from one place. Probe
// came in S19; Scale, Paint, Measure, Slice and Rotate come in S22 (E and R are kept for Rotate
// and Scale).
//
//   snap_step  the Move tool's snap and the transform session's step, metres
//   tools      in the palette's order (down a column, or along a row at a top or bottom edge):
//              id, label (the tool's one name: palette tooltip, menus, ? sheet),
//              behaviour (which also picks the button's icon), about (its tooltip's second line),
//              variants (optional): where the tool's flyout takes its choices from. A tool with
//                variants shows a corner mark; holding its button (0.4 s), a right-click, or its
//                "variants" stop from the keyboard opens the flyout; choosing one runs
//                `tool <id> <variant>`. Sources the code knows (`tools::Variants`):
//                  Starters   the starters of scenes/starters.ron (what Place puts down)
// Snap is not a tool: it is a setting of Move, a switch in the options row under the viewport's
// header while Move is in hand (the action `snap`, S, Edit menu).
(
    snap_step: 0.25,
    tools: [
        (
            id: "select",
            label: "Select",
            behaviour: Select,
            about: "click a body or a tower to select it; drag a body to move it in the view's plane",
        ),
        (
            id: "move",
            label: "Move",
            behaviour: Translate,
            about: "a gizmo on the selected body: drag an arrow to move it along x, y or z, snapped; drag the square to move it freely",
        ),
        (
            id: "place",
            label: "Place",
            behaviour: Place,
            about: "click the ground to add the chosen starter there; hold or right-click to choose it",
            variants: Starters,
        ),
        (
            id: "probe",
            label: "Probe",
            behaviour: Probe,
            about: "click a point: the bodies' gravity there, the voxel cell and its share of each tower's phase",
        ),
    ],
)
